{
  "date": "2026-11-12",
  "purpose": "Implement narrow DOM updates for live game changes and remove redundant background status work.",
  "changes": [
    "Subscribed call-status stream sends per-location/per-game patches after the initial full snapshot; no parallel polling during ordinary updates; missing revisions trigger a full resubscription.",
    "Immutable server projections reuse equal diagnoses and yield cooperatively; sockets without subscriptions receive no call-status background messages.",
    "Boundary labels use native table cells aligned with the teams column; application geometry reads and forced boundary layout were removed.",
    "Per-player/team/official updates preserve unaffected names, check-in controls, resource hints, badges and timer handles.",
    "Paired tablet operator labels update individual members; aggregated attendance changes only when its displayed value changes.",
    "Count badges, todo entries, call-status rule groups and assignment options retain their nodes; minimum moves retain ordered subsequences of games/options/devices.",
    "Tablet waiting entries and their input form are retained; edits preserve focus, selection, input and unrelated entries.",
    "Compact official rotation retains cards, drop targets and timer handles; retained handlers use fresh server records. Real browser drag-and-drop remains verified.",
    "Cancelled/coalesced status reads release their tracked UI jobs after subscription, tournament change or connection loss."
  ],
